"science supports that
this is the way it happens

00:30:42.557 --> 00:30:45.510
"in a free country where
people can choose."

00:30:45.510 --> 00:30:47.530
And we had one of the
top-level politicians

00:30:47.530 --> 00:30:50.280
there and she was, "Well
I don't agree with that."

00:30:50.280 --> 00:30:51.770
And you know I was just,
(Dave laughs)

00:30:51.770 --> 00:30:54.550
I actually made an episode
on my show about that

00:30:54.550 --> 00:30:57.727
because I'm like, "This man
just said 'Science says this.'

00:30:57.727 --> 00:30:58.860
"'I don't agree with it.'"

00:30:58.860 --> 00:31:00.769
Okay, so what are we now, mystics?

00:31:00.769 --> 00:31:02.580
- So what you're saying is--
- Well we are, yeah.

00:31:02.580 --> 00:31:05.430
- Yeah, so that thing though,

00:31:05.430 --> 00:31:07.097
the politician says that,
"I don't agree with it.

00:31:07.097 --> 00:31:08.397
"I don't agree with what science says,

00:31:08.397 --> 00:31:09.810
"I don't agree with what biology says."

00:31:09.810 --> 00:31:11.300
We all know that men
and women are different

00:31:11.300 --> 00:31:13.630
it doesn't make either
sex better than the other

00:31:13.630 --> 00:31:15.650
it's just an is.
- No.

00:31:15.650 --> 00:31:17.160
- But when you hear
that response you think

00:31:17.160 --> 00:31:19.010
most people just swallow that and take it?

00:31:19.010 --> 00:31:20.760
- I think most people
do that because we're

00:31:20.760 --> 00:31:23.610
a fiercely egalitarian,
very conformist people.

00:31:23.610 --> 00:31:26.080
So they have been trained for very long

00:31:26.080 --> 00:31:29.020
to just accept that form of communication.

00:31:29.020 --> 00:31:32.500
Now we have, you know, a government body

00:31:32.500 --> 00:31:36.620
the Ministry of Equality,
and I mean just the name

00:31:36.620 --> 00:31:38.187
sounds so totalitarian I
can't, you know it's like--

00:31:39.217 --> 00:31:40.350
- "Nineteen Eighty-Four" event.

00:31:40.350 --> 00:31:43.350
- Totally, and they have the authority

00:31:43.350 --> 00:31:47.620
to look at all companies and
other governmental bodies

00:31:47.620 --> 00:31:49.850
to achieve the 50/50.
- Kindergartens, schools,

00:31:49.850 --> 00:31:52.090
universities, everything.

00:31:52.090 --> 00:31:54.130
Everything has to be gender mainstreamed.

00:31:54.130 --> 00:31:55.360
- And is all run by women. (laughs)

00:31:55.360 --> 00:31:57.430
There are only women working at the--

00:31:57.430 --> 00:31:59.860
- So right, so when you do this then

00:31:59.860 --> 00:32:03.160
as a private businessman,
how does that affect you?

00:32:03.160 --> 00:32:04.506
- You know, funny thing is like

00:32:04.506 --> 00:32:07.520
when my YouTube channel started taking off

00:32:07.520 --> 00:32:10.210
my business partner he was
like, "Okay, what's happening,

00:32:10.210 --> 00:32:11.043
"what's going on?

00:32:11.043 --> 00:32:13.940
"This might actually hurt
our business interests."

00:32:13.940 --> 00:32:16.627
And I said, "Well you
know, if we start seeing

00:32:16.627 --> 00:32:21.257
"some disasters happening
because of what I'm saying online

00:32:21.257 --> 00:32:22.457
"we'll have a conversation
and say, 'Okay.'"

00:32:22.457 --> 00:32:24.320
And so we tried it for a while,

00:32:24.320 --> 00:32:27.020
turns out business is booming

00:32:27.020 --> 00:32:30.340
because now people are finding me

00:32:30.340 --> 00:32:32.107
just because they see
my videos and, "I wanna

00:32:32.107 --> 00:32:33.570
"work with your company."

00:32:33.570 --> 00:32:35.850
So even though we have
all these enemies now,

00:32:35.850 --> 00:32:36.790
those are people I wouldn't

00:32:36.790 --> 00:32:37.740
wanna work with anyway. (chuckles)

00:32:37.740 --> 00:32:39.500
- Right, but what about
on the hiring side though?

00:32:39.500 --> 00:32:42.300
I mean, when you're actually hiring people

00:32:42.300 --> 00:32:45.440
do you have to look at those
immutable characteristics

00:32:45.440 --> 00:32:46.690
to figure out who you're gonna hire?

00:32:46.690 --> 00:32:49.680
- Well I don't handle the
recruiting any more personally

00:32:49.680 --> 00:32:52.923
so I've kind of removed myself,
my face, from that a bit.

00:32:54.000 --> 00:32:55.570
I don't think it's much of a problem

00:32:55.570 --> 00:32:57.360
because Sweden has a general problem

00:32:57.360 --> 00:32:59.080
when it comes to
recruiting talented people,

00:32:59.080 --> 00:33:00.300
we don't have enough of them.

00:33:00.300 --> 00:33:02.120
We have a lot of people that are going,

00:33:02.120 --> 00:33:05.370
you know, subsidies and various
government programs, loads.

00:33:05.370 --> 00:33:08.873
But I'm in IT recruiting
very smart IT professionals.

00:33:08.873 --> 00:33:11.520
That's generally very difficult.

00:33:11.520 --> 00:33:14.900
Although, I find I have
quite a few of them,

00:33:14.900 --> 00:33:18.430
you know, these software guys
that are quite libertarian.

00:33:18.430 --> 00:33:23.400
So no, I don't see it as
a great problem, you know?

00:33:23.400 --> 00:33:26.780
Here's another thing I'd like to mention,

00:33:26.780 --> 00:33:29.290
you're not allowed to ask
people anything you want

00:33:29.290 --> 00:33:31.120
when you hire them in Sweden.

00:33:31.120 --> 00:33:33.490
So when I first started out my company

00:33:33.490 --> 00:33:35.487
I would ask people, "Are you in any unions

00:33:35.487 --> 00:33:39.060
"because I don't want any
unionized people in my companies."

00:33:39.060 --> 00:33:41.387
And then my HR eventually,
"You gotta stop saying

00:33:41.387 --> 00:33:42.637
"that Henrik, it's illegal.

00:33:42.637 --> 00:33:44.867
"You cannot ask them
if they're unionized."

00:33:45.810 --> 00:33:48.470
So now we have a text in when we recruit

00:33:48.470 --> 00:33:50.617
which is kind of like, "Are you a very

00:33:50.617 --> 00:33:52.687
"collectivistically-minded person?

00:33:52.687 --> 00:33:54.760
"This might not be the place for you."

00:33:54.760 --> 00:33:57.220
- Yeah geez, I mean this is happening

00:33:57.220 --> 00:33:58.600
everywhere now, so nothing

00:33:58.600 --> 00:33:59.790
sort of surprises.
- No, but I think

00:33:59.790 --> 00:34:02.210
it does hurt kids because if you raise

00:34:02.210 --> 00:34:03.900
entire generations of girls

00:34:03.900 --> 00:34:05.850
telling them that they are beautiful

00:34:05.850 --> 00:34:09.010
and weak and strong at the
same time and can do no wrong,

00:34:09.010 --> 00:34:12.130
well you're turning them into
sexist fascists basically

00:34:12.130 --> 00:34:13.470
and you're telling all the boys

00:34:13.470 --> 00:34:14.970
that they are inherently evil,

00:34:14.970 --> 00:34:18.110
and we've been doing
this for a long time now.

00:34:18.110 --> 00:34:19.880
- So is that the part that's particularly

00:34:19.880 --> 00:34:20.790
perverse about this?

00:34:20.790 --> 00:34:22.370
You take a society, you make them equal.

00:34:22.370 --> 00:34:24.020
Then at the same time because you know

00:34:24.020 --> 00:34:26.100
that humans are gonna
have individual emotions

00:34:26.100 --> 00:34:29.900
you keep telling the
males that they're evil

00:34:29.900 --> 00:34:31.640
despite the fact that you in Sweden

00:34:31.640 --> 00:34:35.470
have done more for equality
than virtually anybody.

00:34:35.470 --> 00:34:37.740
So it's really like
it's just never enough,

00:34:37.740 --> 00:34:39.130
because actually as you guys know

00:34:39.130 --> 00:34:41.150
what they want is not really equality,

00:34:41.150 --> 00:34:42.380
it's some sort of--
- No, no.

00:34:42.380 --> 00:34:44.210
- Conformity is what they want.

00:34:44.210 --> 00:34:45.720
- And I've been trying to tell them

00:34:45.720 --> 00:34:49.110
that this would be as if
someone came out as gay

00:34:49.110 --> 00:34:52.000
and you told them, "No,
suppress that" right?

00:34:52.000 --> 00:34:54.060
Because that's what
you're telling the boys.

00:34:54.060 --> 00:34:55.257
Like, "Oh, you feel the need the need

00:34:55.257 --> 00:34:59.014
"to run around and play
football, suppress it."

00:34:59.014 --> 00:34:59.847
- "You're a smart girl."
- And you're telling

00:34:59.847 --> 00:35:00.877
the girls like, "You're playing

00:35:00.877 --> 00:35:02.777
"with dolls, bad girl.

00:35:02.777 --> 00:35:04.070
"Go out and play football."

00:35:04.070 --> 00:35:06.217
- Now before the haters
get in here and say,

00:35:06.217 --> 00:35:09.060
"Oh Aron Flam doesn't want
boys to play with Barbies"

00:35:09.060 --> 00:35:10.710
you actually are perfectly okay if they--

00:35:10.710 --> 00:35:12.120
- I never played football.

00:35:12.120 --> 00:35:13.386
I was not the type.
(Dave laughs)

00:35:13.386 --> 00:35:14.219
- And you had the

00:35:14.219 --> 00:35:15.769
huge Barbie collection.
(Henrik laughs)

00:35:15.769 --> 00:35:17.150
- Well.
- Which for a man

00:35:17.150 --> 00:35:18.316
of your age is a bit much now.

00:35:18.316 --> 00:35:22.470
- (laughs) I was into He-Man
and Star Wars figurines.

00:35:22.470 --> 00:35:24.540
Or action--
- Action figures.

00:35:24.540 --> 00:35:26.220
- Yes, you call them that to make them

00:35:26.220 --> 00:35:28.650
sound more manly, but
they're basically dolls.

00:35:28.650 --> 00:35:30.470
- I'll show you my collection

00:35:30.470 --> 00:35:31.540
when we're outta here.
(Henrik laughs)

00:35:31.540 --> 00:35:34.090
All right let's shift a bit
because you mentioned actually

00:35:34.090 --> 00:35:38.640
that you lived and I
believe you're moving,

00:35:38.640 --> 00:35:40.000
if I can say that--
- Yes.

00:35:40.000 --> 00:35:42.300
In Malmo, now we here a lot about Malmo

00:35:42.300 --> 00:35:44.640
on a certain side of the internet

00:35:44.640 --> 00:35:46.810
where they report on a lot of bombings

00:35:46.810 --> 00:35:48.730
and stabbings and all these weird things

00:35:48.730 --> 00:35:49.890
coming outta Malmo.

00:35:49.890 --> 00:35:52.693
Now we only hear of
this from sort of right,

00:35:52.693 --> 00:35:54.870
what I would say are not just center right

00:35:54.870 --> 00:35:58.090
but more right-leaning
things, outlets in America.

00:35:58.090 --> 00:36:00.410
And then anyone that reports on them

00:36:00.410 --> 00:36:02.460
says that they're racist
and they're bigoted

00:36:02.460 --> 00:36:03.970
and the rest of it.

00:36:03.970 --> 00:36:06.700
You live in Malmo, what happened in Malmo?

00:36:06.700 --> 00:36:08.480
And just tell me a little bit
about the history of Malmo

00:36:08.480 --> 00:36:09.810
before anything else.

00:36:09.810 --> 00:36:12.303
- Malmo, it's in the deep south of Sweden.

00:36:13.450 --> 00:36:16.180
So it's a port city and this is where

00:36:16.180 --> 00:36:18.670
basically everyone that's coming to Sweden

00:36:18.670 --> 00:36:21.820
by foot or by car, they
will enter across a bridge

00:36:21.820 --> 00:36:23.220
and they come into Malmo

00:36:23.220 --> 00:36:27.050
so we have a very large number of refugees

00:36:27.050 --> 00:36:30.330
and so forth from the crisis of 2015.

00:36:30.330 --> 00:36:33.660
And Malmo, it's always been
a rather poor city, you know?

00:36:33.660 --> 00:36:35.370
They used to build big ships there

00:36:35.370 --> 00:36:37.270
and then in the 1980s that all collapsed

00:36:37.270 --> 00:36:39.300
and everyone was an alcoholic for a while.

00:36:39.300 --> 00:36:41.140
Then it kind of became slightly better

00:36:41.140 --> 00:36:43.590
but it's a loss-making city

00:36:43.590 --> 00:36:46.420
and it's been run by
socialists for you know,

00:36:46.420 --> 00:36:48.960
better part of the last hundred years.

00:36:48.960 --> 00:36:53.960
Now over time, crime in Malmo
started to rise uncontrollably

00:36:56.390 --> 00:37:00.840
and again, coming back to
the same topic all the time,

00:37:00.840 --> 00:37:04.150
this concept of being quiet
about what is happening

00:37:04.150 --> 00:37:06.280
because it's considered rude to mention

00:37:06.280 --> 00:37:09.530
the fact that well, we
might have a drug war

00:37:09.530 --> 00:37:12.240
going on in this city, and
that's what we have right now.

00:37:12.240 --> 00:37:15.940
So people are working
very hard at putting out

00:37:15.940 --> 00:37:17.690
different kind of representations,

00:37:17.690 --> 00:37:20.190
statistical representations
saying, "everything is fine"

00:37:20.190 --> 00:37:21.700
but you know, it's
getting harder and harder

00:37:21.700 --> 00:37:25.270
for them to do that because everyone knows

00:37:25.270 --> 00:37:28.800
that we did not use to have weekly bombs

00:37:28.800 --> 00:37:31.730
going off in the city
center, for one thing.

00:37:31.730 --> 00:37:35.030
And if I can, I'd like
to sort of tie this back

00:37:35.030 --> 00:37:37.220
to a personal experience.

00:37:37.220 --> 00:37:40.000
You mentioned that time
that I was burglarized

00:37:40.000 --> 00:37:41.630
and what's really
interesting about that story

00:37:41.630 --> 00:37:43.680
is not so much the fact
that I was burglarized

00:37:43.680 --> 00:37:46.540
but rather the reaction
I got from the media

00:37:46.540 --> 00:37:47.750
when I wrote about this

00:37:47.750 --> 00:37:49.000
in the paper.
- And from the police

00:37:49.000 --> 00:37:51.040
when you asked them, "What
can I do about this?"

00:37:51.040 --> 00:37:51.950
So please, go on.
- Yeah, this is

00:37:51.950 --> 00:37:52.783
an incredible story, please tell it.

00:37:52.783 --> 00:37:54.620
- I'll just make it really short you know.

00:37:54.620 --> 00:37:56.170
I wake up in the middle of the night,

00:37:56.170 --> 00:37:57.630
somebody's trying to break into our house.

00:37:57.630 --> 00:38:01.540
I carry my twin girls upstairs,

00:38:01.540 --> 00:38:03.430
arm myself with a hammer
because I didn't have

00:38:03.430 --> 00:38:04.520
a gun at home.

00:38:04.520 --> 00:38:06.340
Hammer, I'm on the phone with the police.

00:38:06.340 --> 00:38:08.850
They're trying to force
entry through our front door

00:38:08.850 --> 00:38:10.347
and the police are saying, "Be quiet.

00:38:10.347 --> 00:38:11.727
"Don't make your presence known,

00:38:11.727 --> 00:38:13.090
"we'll be there shortly."

00:38:13.090 --> 00:38:14.080
Then my neighbor comes home,

00:38:14.080 --> 00:38:16.670
we have a shared walkway,
he scared them off

00:38:16.670 --> 00:38:19.550
by turning on the lights so they got away.

00:38:19.550 --> 00:38:22.691
30 minutes later I'm giving my testimony,

00:38:22.691 --> 00:38:23.547
is that what you say?
- Mm-hm.

00:38:23.547 --> 00:38:26.430
- Statement to the police
sitting in my kitchen

00:38:26.430 --> 00:38:28.080
and I ask him at the end of the interview,

00:38:28.080 --> 00:38:31.143
it's like, "So what can
I do to protect myself

00:38:31.143 --> 00:38:33.890
"and my family from this
ever happening again?"

00:38:33.890 --> 00:38:38.697
And literally he does
this, "(sighs) Seriously?

00:38:38.697 --> 00:38:40.187
"Don't live in this city.

00:38:40.187 --> 00:38:42.730
"It is out of control,
we cannot control it."

00:38:42.730 --> 00:38:45.380
This was in 2007, you know?

00:38:45.380 --> 00:38:46.970
That year I think I believe I paid

00:38:46.970 --> 00:38:49.390
about 12 million in taxes and I live

00:38:49.390 --> 00:38:51.460
in a fashionable part of town

00:38:51.460 --> 00:38:54.510
as I expect a better answer.
- I've been to his penthouse.

00:38:54.510 --> 00:38:55.940
It's very nice, yes, yeah.
- Yeah.

00:38:55.940 --> 00:38:56.780
- That's where I interviewed you.

00:38:56.780 --> 00:38:58.070
- Yeah.
(Dave laughs)

00:38:58.070 --> 00:39:00.560
- I expect a better answer by the police

00:39:00.560 --> 00:39:02.180
than them telling me to leave.

00:39:02.180 --> 00:39:04.570
So I wrote an editorial about this

00:39:04.570 --> 00:39:08.540
in Sweden's largest conservative newspaper

00:39:08.540 --> 00:39:11.980
and told the story about the, basically

00:39:11.980 --> 00:39:13.710
what the policeman told
me which is (murmurs)

00:39:13.710 --> 00:39:16.380
that this is the really shocking part.

00:39:16.380 --> 00:39:20.480
The reaction by the local
newspaper in Malmo was,

00:39:20.480 --> 00:39:21.500
they didn't speak to me,

00:39:21.500 --> 00:39:23.620
they spoke to the paper
that took my editorial

00:39:23.620 --> 00:39:26.127
and said, "This is
completely unacceptable.

00:39:26.127 --> 00:39:29.997
"What poor taste and
journalistic unprofessionalism

00:39:29.997 --> 00:39:33.487
"that you should publish
an alarmist, populistic

00:39:33.487 --> 00:39:35.487
"text like this which
is drawing the attention

00:39:35.487 --> 00:39:37.387
"from the people in need.

00:39:37.387 --> 00:39:40.287
"This is a wealthy capitalist.

00:39:40.287 --> 00:39:45.287
"He's spoiled and you should
not listen to this alarmism."

00:39:45.580 --> 00:39:48.150
And that really shocked me
because I had journalists

00:39:48.150 --> 00:39:49.973
attacking me on Facebook,
"Why do you write that?

00:39:49.973 --> 00:39:53.800
"Why do you put a text
like that out there?"

00:39:53.800 --> 00:39:56.037
And this was just when I was
starting my YouTube channel

00:39:56.037 --> 00:39:57.650
so this--
- And then you got called

00:39:57.650 --> 00:39:59.546
racist and the rest of it, right?

00:39:59.546 --> 00:40:00.480
All that stuff.
- Racist, fascist.

00:40:00.480 --> 00:40:02.110
- Goes without saying.
- Bigoted.

00:40:02.110 --> 00:40:05.070
Right-wing, nut job, you know.

00:40:05.070 --> 00:40:06.111
They didn't, they had

00:40:06.111 --> 00:40:06.944
to start using--
- White supremacist.

00:40:06.944 --> 00:40:08.490
- The word whore.
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:40:08.490 --> 00:40:09.570
- But so all this being said,

00:40:09.570 --> 00:40:12.300
you stayed in Malmo for
two years basically.

00:40:12.300 --> 00:40:13.619
- Well he's not Jewish. (laughs)

00:40:13.619 --> 00:40:14.452
- Yeah (laughs) right.
(Henrik laughs)

00:40:14.452 --> 00:40:16.051
So we'll get to that
(Aron laughs)

00:40:16.051 --> 00:40:17.468
in just a second.

00:40:18.650 --> 00:40:19.530
But you stayed?

00:40:19.530 --> 00:40:21.440
- Yeah, we stayed.

00:40:21.440 --> 00:40:24.320
The crime situation has escalated so

00:40:24.320 --> 00:40:27.630
when we finally, the straw
that broke the camel's back

00:40:27.630 --> 00:40:30.770
was this summer, and I
made a video about this.

00:40:30.770 --> 00:40:34.470
It was so tragic because
these drug cartels

00:40:34.470 --> 00:40:36.920
are basically fighting it out in Malmo.

00:40:36.920 --> 00:40:40.240
They shot a young mother in the head

00:40:40.240 --> 00:40:43.090
while she was carrying, and
I can hardly speak about this

00:40:43.090 --> 00:40:45.260
because it really upsets me to be honest.

00:40:45.260 --> 00:40:46.710
They shot her dead in the head

00:40:46.710 --> 00:40:48.660
while she was carrying her newborn baby

00:40:48.660 --> 00:40:51.520
because she was affiliated
with one of the drug gangs

00:40:51.520 --> 00:40:53.680
and there was a trial thing going on.

00:40:53.680 --> 00:40:55.946
This was nine o'clock in the morning

00:40:55.946 --> 00:40:59.400
on a public street in one of
the most affluent neighborhoods

00:40:59.400 --> 00:41:03.220
in the city and it just
really broke me, honestly.

00:41:03.220 --> 00:41:05.604
I am not raising my children in this city

00:41:05.604 --> 00:41:07.977
so now we're looking for
a house outside the city.

00:41:07.977 --> 00:41:09.793
- So you're on your way out.

00:41:11.260 --> 00:41:14.300
As the representative of all
Jewish people in Sweden--

00:41:14.300 --> 00:41:15.218
- Please, they would like

00:41:15.218 --> 00:41:17.214
that at all.
(Henrik laughs)

00:41:17.214 --> 00:41:18.980
- I bet you secretly they would.

00:41:18.980 --> 00:41:20.820
Maybe they wouldn't want--

00:41:20.820 --> 00:41:22.307
- Who knows, there's--
- neighbors to know.

00:41:22.307 --> 00:41:24.330
But there's only what, about 7,000 Jews

00:41:24.330 --> 00:41:25.470
left in Sweden, is that right?

00:41:25.470 --> 00:41:27.330
- Maybe eight, I don't know.

00:41:27.330 --> 00:41:28.800
It fluctuates nowadays.

00:41:28.800 --> 00:41:30.787
- Yeah, but can you sort of
explain what's happening?

00:41:30.787 --> 00:41:33.720
- But Malmo used to have
a vibrant Jewish community

00:41:33.720 --> 00:41:36.740
of around 3,000 Jews.
- My best friend was a Jew.

00:41:36.740 --> 00:41:39.090
- For a hundred years and by now

00:41:39.090 --> 00:41:41.610
there's probably maybe 300 Jews left.

00:41:41.610 --> 00:41:44.350
They've all left Malmo
in the last few yeas.

00:41:44.350 --> 00:41:46.300
They go either to
Stockholm if they're young

00:41:46.300 --> 00:41:51.300
or if they can to America
or Canada or Israel.

00:41:51.650 --> 00:41:53.970
So they've evacuated the city pretty much

00:41:53.970 --> 00:41:57.350
and it has gone so far that
two private individuals

00:41:57.350 --> 00:42:00.600
donated 40 million of their own money

00:42:00.600 --> 00:42:02.690
to the Jewish congregation so that they

00:42:02.690 --> 00:42:06.080
can manage security fort
the 300 individuals left

00:42:06.080 --> 00:42:07.730
just for the coming 10 years.

00:42:07.730 --> 00:42:09.303
- One of them was Dan Olofsson, right?

00:42:09.303 --> 00:42:10.270
- That you have interviewed.

00:42:10.270 --> 00:42:11.443
- He was on my show.
- I know.

00:42:11.443 --> 00:42:13.100
- And I'm hoping to get
him on your show as well.

00:42:13.100 --> 00:42:15.290
- Yes, but we will talk
about different subjects.

00:42:15.290 --> 00:42:16.850
You talked about entrepreneurship

00:42:16.850 --> 00:42:17.683
and I will talk about--

00:42:17.683 --> 00:42:18.910
- Oh he's a massive entrepreneur.

00:42:18.910 --> 00:42:20.260
- Yeah, he is.
- A super talented guy.

00:42:20.260 --> 00:42:22.397
- Well you'd have to
be to donate 20 million

00:42:22.397 --> 00:42:25.700
out of your own pocket to found

00:42:27.100 --> 00:42:28.900
Sweden's first private militia

00:42:28.900 --> 00:42:31.230
which is basically what it will become.

00:42:31.230 --> 00:42:33.500
- Can you explain sort of,
so you were talking about

00:42:33.500 --> 00:42:35.383
kinda gang violence and that sorta thing.

00:42:35.383 --> 00:42:37.710
But can you explain how
that's sort of related

00:42:37.710 --> 00:42:40.020
to why Jews would be
getting out specifically?

00:42:40.020 --> 00:42:40.890
- Absolutely.
- 'Cause now we're seeing this

00:42:40.890 --> 00:42:42.100
sort of all over Europe and--

00:42:42.100 --> 00:42:42.990
- No problem at all.

00:42:42.990 --> 00:42:46.200
So we've had a huge influx of immigration

00:42:46.200 --> 00:42:49.400
from poor Middle Eastern
and North African countries

00:42:49.400 --> 00:42:51.370
where state anti-Semitism is part

00:42:51.370 --> 00:42:53.800
of everyday life growing up.

00:42:53.800 --> 00:42:57.170
So they come to us and
they're still anti-Semites

00:42:57.170 --> 00:43:00.260
and the socialists of Sweden,
being on Hitler's side

00:43:00.260 --> 00:43:01.700
until the end of the World War

00:43:01.700 --> 00:43:04.680
and never dealing with
that have been, you know,

00:43:04.680 --> 00:43:07.970
it's a low simmering sort of thing

00:43:07.970 --> 00:43:09.300
that they never dealt with.

00:43:09.300 --> 00:43:11.760
And they have an alliance

00:43:11.760 --> 00:43:14.560
and they don't care if the Jews are

00:43:16.080 --> 00:43:17.510
forced out of the city.

00:43:17.510 --> 00:43:21.180
That's just, yeah?
- We need to mention

00:43:21.180 --> 00:43:24.170
that the government of,
well the Social Democrats

00:43:24.170 --> 00:43:25.850
who've been ruling for a long time,

00:43:25.850 --> 00:43:28.760
they are actively siding with Palestine

00:43:28.760 --> 00:43:30.820
in the Middle Eastern question.

00:43:30.820 --> 00:43:32.420
- Yep.
- And you know,

00:43:32.420 --> 00:43:34.400
the historical, this goes way back

00:43:34.400 --> 00:43:35.490
but it has something to do with

00:43:35.490 --> 00:43:37.530
Israel being in cahoots with America

00:43:37.530 --> 00:43:40.520
and America's the great Satan so then

00:43:40.520 --> 00:43:41.830
because if you're a socialist

00:43:41.830 --> 00:43:43.409
being oppressed is a currency.

00:43:43.409 --> 00:43:45.430
The Palestinians are the more oppressed

00:43:45.430 --> 00:43:46.870
so they side with them.

00:43:46.870 --> 00:43:49.670
But we have the youth organization

00:43:49.670 --> 00:43:51.090
of the Social Democratic Party,

00:43:51.090 --> 00:43:52.050
and I'll send you a video of this

00:43:52.050 --> 00:43:54.370
so you can see it for yourself.

00:43:54.370 --> 00:43:56.730
When they demonstrate,
like on the 1st of May

00:43:56.730 --> 00:43:58.650
they have like a socialist holiday

00:43:58.650 --> 00:44:00.080
where they celebrate I don't know,

00:44:00.080 --> 00:44:02.470
whatever socialists celebrate.

00:44:02.470 --> 00:44:03.303
- Potato day? (laughs)

00:44:03.303 --> 00:44:04.755
Whadda socialists celebrate?

00:44:04.755 --> 00:44:07.960
- No, we have 1st of May is
International Workers' Day.

00:44:07.960 --> 00:44:10.222
They celebrate being poor as well.

00:44:10.222 --> 00:44:12.200
(Dave laughs)
(Aron laughs)

00:44:12.200 --> 00:44:14.650
- And they--
- Now they will hate me more.

00:44:14.650 --> 00:44:16.941
- They sang, and this is on video,

00:44:16.941 --> 00:44:18.906
the last time the demonstration--

00:44:18.906 --> 00:44:19.739
- They always sing that song.
- Walks through the city.

00:44:19.739 --> 00:44:21.307
- It just got caught on tape?

00:44:21.307 --> 00:44:25.557
(Henrik sings in foreign language)

00:44:28.690 --> 00:44:30.200
- I think you can pick out
a couple words right there.

00:44:30.200 --> 00:44:31.720
- Yeah.
- It means, celebrate,

00:44:31.720 --> 00:44:35.000
celebrate, celebrate
Palestine and crush Zionism.

00:44:35.000 --> 00:44:37.777
And this is the Socialist
Youth Organization people.

00:44:37.777 --> 00:44:40.327
These are middle class Swedish people

00:44:40.327 --> 00:44:42.210
and to me that's an outrage.

00:44:42.210 --> 00:44:43.043
It's an outrage.

00:44:43.043 --> 00:44:44.960
They never speak about this.

00:44:44.960 --> 00:44:47.850
- No, and the former strong man of Malmo,

00:44:47.850 --> 00:44:50.340
the Social Democratic leader Ilmar Reepalu

00:44:50.340 --> 00:44:52.400
he had, I mean anti-Semitism.

00:44:52.400 --> 00:44:55.010
He has been accused of
being an anti-Semite for

00:44:56.290 --> 00:45:00.120
decades now, but he always
denied it and by now

00:45:00.120 --> 00:45:03.280
they can't deny it because
there are no Jews left, so.

00:45:03.280 --> 00:45:04.113
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:45:04.113 --> 00:45:05.450
- Can you guys explain a little bit

00:45:05.450 --> 00:45:09.840
about how the immigration issue arose?

00:45:09.840 --> 00:45:12.350
That basically this all
started just in the last

00:45:12.350 --> 00:45:14.520
really seven years, something like that.

00:45:14.520 --> 00:45:17.440
That a pretty much homogenous society

00:45:17.440 --> 00:45:20.840
for better or worse, decided I think

00:45:20.840 --> 00:45:21.673
but correct me if I'm wrong,

00:45:21.673 --> 00:45:23.490
I think probably with good intentions

00:45:23.490 --> 00:45:25.780
by people that weren't thinking that much

00:45:25.780 --> 00:45:27.460
to bring in a ton of people.

00:45:27.460 --> 00:45:28.850
How many immigrants roughly

00:45:28.850 --> 00:45:30.290
have come in over the last--

00:45:30.290 --> 00:45:31.320
- Well--
- Half decade or so?

00:45:31.320 --> 00:45:33.300
- You can take this one I think.

00:45:33.300 --> 00:45:35.073
- If you take it over a decade,

00:45:36.190 --> 00:45:37.970
the numbers are always changing

00:45:37.970 --> 00:45:39.300
because they're playing around with them

00:45:39.300 --> 00:45:41.850
so it depends on how you
kind of calculate it.

00:45:41.850 --> 00:45:44.530
But it is a bit over a million people.

00:45:44.530 --> 00:45:47.430
- Okay, so roughly a
10th of the population

00:45:47.430 --> 00:45:49.900
came in, let's say in the last decade

00:45:49.900 --> 00:45:51.173
from these countries.

00:45:52.190 --> 00:45:54.150
What do you think the leaders thought

00:45:54.150 --> 00:45:55.953
exactly was gonna happen?

00:45:57.390 --> 00:45:58.940
Let's say well-intentioned.

00:45:58.940 --> 00:46:00.607
But do you think maybe I'm
giving them too much credit?

00:46:00.607 --> 00:46:02.720
- No, let's do the well-intentioned

00:46:02.720 --> 00:46:03.780
because I like to give people

00:46:03.780 --> 00:46:05.173
the benefit of the doubt.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:46:05.173 --> 00:46:09.640
- I think they were hoping
for a multi-cultural nirvana

00:46:09.640 --> 00:46:14.611
with, you know, kebabs
and some belly dancing

00:46:14.611 --> 00:46:17.130
and that everyone else--
- And a lotta smoked fish.

00:46:17.130 --> 00:46:17.963
You guys are killin' it
(Henrik laughs)

00:46:17.963 --> 00:46:19.216
in the smoked fish game by the way.

00:46:19.216 --> 00:46:20.049
- We do have it.
- I ate some

00:46:20.049 --> 00:46:20.990
delicious outta that.

00:46:20.990 --> 00:46:21.823
- That is true.
- Yeah.

00:46:21.823 --> 00:46:24.420
- But other than that, I think the idea

00:46:24.420 --> 00:46:28.580
is if you live in a culture
that is so homogenous

00:46:28.580 --> 00:46:31.440
as Sweden is, you cannot
think outside the box

00:46:31.440 --> 00:46:32.500
of our own culture.

00:46:32.500 --> 00:46:35.090
They don't even perceive
that we have a culture.

00:46:35.090 --> 00:46:38.890
They probably believe
they will become Swedes

00:46:38.890 --> 00:46:40.280
very quickly when they realize

00:46:40.280 --> 00:46:42.400
how right a good we are.
- Yes, they will become--

00:46:42.400 --> 00:46:44.910
- Turns out didn't happen.
- Yeah.

00:46:44.910 --> 00:46:45.743
- Yeah, so if we were not to give them

00:46:45.743 --> 00:46:48.330
the benefit of the doubt, because I also,

00:46:48.330 --> 00:46:49.930
I try not to go to people's motives

00:46:49.930 --> 00:46:51.040
and I think the road to hell is paved

00:46:51.040 --> 00:46:53.130
with good intentions and I
think a lot of these people

00:46:53.130 --> 00:46:54.246
think they're doing the right thing.

00:46:54.246 --> 00:46:57.024
But let's go to the non-good motive part.

00:46:57.024 --> 00:46:58.530
(Henrik laughs)
Because I think you just

00:46:58.530 --> 00:46:59.520
wrote a book about it.
- Yes.

00:46:59.520 --> 00:47:01.270
- I mean, what do you think these people

00:47:01.270 --> 00:47:02.350
thought they were doing?

00:47:02.350 --> 00:47:03.750
Or whadda you think they thought

00:47:03.750 --> 00:47:05.320
was going to happen?

00:47:05.320 --> 00:47:07.667
Just when you change
demographics that much,

00:47:07.667 --> 00:47:11.200
a 10th of a population is
a huge, huge, huge amount.

00:47:11.200 --> 00:47:13.763
- Well I think they wanted to,

00:47:14.620 --> 00:47:17.200
so the Social Democrat came into power.

00:47:17.200 --> 00:47:19.370
They actually lifted up the working class

00:47:19.370 --> 00:47:21.820
to a much better living standard

00:47:21.820 --> 00:47:23.760
and the idea was as soon as we get them

00:47:23.760 --> 00:47:25.610
up to middle class living standards

00:47:25.610 --> 00:47:28.020
they will become true
Communists and understand

00:47:28.020 --> 00:47:30.810
that they need to devote
everything to the struggle.

00:47:30.810 --> 00:47:33.280
What happened in reality was that they

00:47:33.280 --> 00:47:35.590
were perfectly fine with
their flat screen TVs.

00:47:35.590 --> 00:47:38.500
They wanted more flat screen
TVs and longer vacation time.

00:47:38.500 --> 00:47:40.830
They didn't want to join
a Communist revolution.

00:47:40.830 --> 00:47:45.160
They became, in essence,
well our equivalent

00:47:45.160 --> 00:47:46.680
of Republicans I suppose.

00:47:46.680 --> 00:47:50.040
So they needed new voters in a sense.

00:47:50.040 --> 00:47:52.520
And they invoked, and then they took in

00:47:52.520 --> 00:47:55.530
a lot of people into
the most over-regulated

00:47:55.530 --> 00:47:58.480
labor market in the world and these people

00:47:58.480 --> 00:48:00.960
second generation and third
generation immigrants,

00:48:00.960 --> 00:48:02.300
they're not getting into the system,

00:48:02.300 --> 00:48:05.050
they're keeping them for the ballots.

00:48:05.050 --> 00:48:08.190
They want their votes and
they keep them on subsidies

00:48:08.190 --> 00:48:10.690
and some of these kids
they see that the system

00:48:10.690 --> 00:48:13.360
is rigged against them
and they have no choice.

00:48:13.360 --> 00:48:14.870
Of course they will become gangsters

00:48:14.870 --> 00:48:17.070
or go off and fight
for ISIS after a while.

00:48:17.070 --> 00:48:18.390
Not all of them, obviously.

00:48:18.390 --> 00:48:20.420
- I think it's important at this point

00:48:20.420 --> 00:48:25.260
to remember that the people that came in,

00:48:25.260 --> 00:48:27.570
you know, those individuals

00:48:27.570 --> 00:48:29.800
it's not their fault inherently, you know?

00:48:29.800 --> 00:48:31.109
- Yeah, they were invited.

00:48:31.109 --> 00:48:32.700
- Well that's why I asked
about the intentions

00:48:32.700 --> 00:48:34.790
and good or bad, of the
people that brought them in.

00:48:34.790 --> 00:48:35.750
Not these people specifically.

00:48:35.750 --> 00:48:39.750
- I'd like to think, you
know, crowds always go crazy.

00:48:39.750 --> 00:48:42.390
But individuals are much
more reasonable, you know?

00:48:42.390 --> 00:48:45.150
And somebody who's fleeing a war,

00:48:45.150 --> 00:48:47.240
I have the deepest
sympathy, yes of course.

00:48:47.240 --> 00:48:48.940
I would do the same thing.

00:48:48.940 --> 00:48:51.450
But it is irresponsible if you have

00:48:51.450 --> 00:48:54.080
a so regulated labor market

00:48:54.080 --> 00:48:57.450
and you take in more
people than you can help.

00:48:57.450 --> 00:48:59.560
That is like you're throwing a party

00:48:59.560 --> 00:49:01.120
that goes haywire on Facebook.

00:49:01.120 --> 00:49:02.890
Everyone's invited.
(Aron laughs)

00:49:02.890 --> 00:49:04.640
But you know, I have drinks for 12 people.

00:49:04.640 --> 00:49:06.880
- What did they think
that people were gonna do?

00:49:06.880 --> 00:49:08.450
Like what kinda jobs did they think

00:49:08.450 --> 00:49:09.283
people were gonna have?

00:49:09.283 --> 00:49:10.997
Or did they immediately
say, "You're taken care of

00:49:10.997 --> 00:49:12.130
"for a year", you know?

00:49:12.130 --> 00:49:12.963
We hear these stories out

00:49:12.963 --> 00:49:13.796
of Germany where--
- Well the government

00:49:13.796 --> 00:49:16.216
wanted to start a camel
farm in Gothenburg.

00:49:16.216 --> 00:49:18.830
- Well that was one experiment for some

00:49:18.830 --> 00:49:21.233
and that's a, yeah, that was crazy.

00:49:22.490 --> 00:49:23.323
- That actually sounds

00:49:23.323 --> 00:49:25.200
like satire, but--
- And sort of racist.

00:49:25.200 --> 00:49:26.897
- Yeah.
- But, "No, we can't

00:49:26.897 --> 00:49:29.387
"give you a proper job but
we'll give you some subsidies.

00:49:29.387 --> 00:49:31.677
"Start a camel farm, you
should be good at that.

00:49:31.677 --> 00:49:34.700
"And also, we have plenty
of camels in Sweden."

00:49:34.700 --> 00:49:35.533
No we don't.

00:49:35.533 --> 00:49:37.530
We have reindeer.
- So truly, people come in

00:49:37.530 --> 00:49:39.370
and as you said they're often fleeing war.

00:49:39.370 --> 00:49:41.020
You have sympathies with all these people.

00:49:41.020 --> 00:49:43.447
The government then
says, "Here's some stuff.

00:49:43.447 --> 00:49:46.260
"But you can't have it forever" although

00:49:46.260 --> 00:49:47.290
they sort of do have it forever.

00:49:47.290 --> 00:49:48.940
But not just the, "Can't have it forever"

00:49:48.940 --> 00:49:50.867
it's a limited amount of stuff, right?

00:49:50.867 --> 00:49:53.410
"We can't put you" and
then they can turn around

00:49:53.410 --> 00:49:54.547
and say, "See, we're also racist

00:49:54.547 --> 00:49:56.700
"'cause we didn't make you
millionaires at night one"

00:49:56.700 --> 00:49:58.330
and the rest of it.
- Exactly.

00:49:58.330 --> 00:49:59.260
They get a flat,

00:49:59.260 --> 00:50:03.260
they get a minimum living--

00:50:03.260 --> 00:50:04.663
- Subsidy.
- Subsidy.

00:50:05.850 --> 00:50:08.890
- And then they are expected to vote left

00:50:08.890 --> 00:50:10.520
and that is what it looks like.

00:50:10.520 --> 00:50:12.250
If you break down the statistics

00:50:12.250 --> 00:50:16.260
of different municipalities
and how they vote.

00:50:16.260 --> 00:50:17.690
I mean in the (speaks in
foreign language) in Malmo

00:50:17.690 --> 00:50:21.700
was like 70 to 90% voted
for the Social Democrat

00:50:21.700 --> 00:50:23.020
of the lefts.
- Yes, yes.

00:50:23.020 --> 00:50:25.560
I mean, you know, we have
the numbers for all of that.

00:50:25.560 --> 00:50:28.290
But what's happened is tragically

00:50:28.290 --> 00:50:31.061
we have created a tremendous segregation.

00:50:31.061 --> 00:50:32.710
- Yeah.
- A new under class

00:50:32.710 --> 00:50:34.860
if you will, an immigrant under class,

00:50:34.860 --> 00:50:36.493
which Sweden never had.

00:50:37.350 --> 00:50:38.627
And we don't know how to deal with it

00:50:38.627 --> 00:50:40.750
and we're also running out of money

00:50:40.750 --> 00:50:43.180
because we have the most
expensive welfare system

00:50:43.180 --> 00:50:45.990
in the world and now we're
trying to deal with it.

00:50:45.990 --> 00:50:47.040
Nobody knows what to do.

00:50:47.040 --> 00:50:49.760
- This is a sort of
dangerous question in a way

00:50:49.760 --> 00:50:52.280
but I think these conversations
always end up here

00:50:52.280 --> 00:50:54.590
which is, do you think in a weird way

00:50:54.590 --> 00:50:56.900
this then breeds racism?
- Yes.

00:50:56.900 --> 00:51:00.040
- That good-intentioned people, right,

00:51:00.040 --> 00:51:01.810
I mean you just made it very clear.

00:51:01.810 --> 00:51:03.860
You have no ill-will towards these people.

00:51:03.860 --> 00:51:05.440
But then these people
come into these countries,

00:51:05.440 --> 00:51:06.540
they're given these things.

00:51:06.540 --> 00:51:09.290
They demand more, the
politicians use them for votes.

00:51:09.290 --> 00:51:11.940
And then good people who are not racist

00:51:11.940 --> 00:51:13.160
but maybe don't have a lotta time

00:51:13.160 --> 00:51:14.210
to think about all these things

00:51:14.210 --> 00:51:16.760
suddenly start becoming kind of racist.

00:51:16.760 --> 00:51:19.430
It's just a sad fact of humanity.

00:51:19.430 --> 00:51:21.450
- Absolutely, and I
think it goes both ways.

00:51:21.450 --> 00:51:24.600
I think the Swedes wanted
to invite poor people

00:51:24.600 --> 00:51:26.600
from the Third World to
come and live in Sweden

00:51:26.600 --> 00:51:29.020
because they wanted to
feel good themselves.

00:51:29.020 --> 00:51:32.207
But also they thought,
"Everyone would want

00:51:32.207 --> 00:51:34.060
"to become Swedish, of course."

00:51:34.060 --> 00:51:36.080
But then they get a lot of immigrants

00:51:36.080 --> 00:51:37.700
and the immigrants look
at the Swedish society

00:51:37.700 --> 00:51:40.187
and they're like, "Eh,
maybe I'm gonna keep

00:51:40.187 --> 00:51:42.417
"some of my own culture", yeah?

00:51:42.417 --> 00:51:44.379
"'Cause I don't think this is so great."

00:51:44.379 --> 00:51:45.350
- And if you were to sort of--

00:51:45.350 --> 00:51:48.190
- And also, if you keep
them out of the system

00:51:48.190 --> 00:51:49.023
and you never left them in

00:51:49.023 --> 00:51:51.070
and you stick them in ghettos,

00:51:51.070 --> 00:51:52.630
of course they will start to hate you.

00:51:52.630 --> 00:51:54.600
- And there's a weird thing
that I think Europe has

00:51:54.600 --> 00:51:55.460
that I think America doesn't have

00:51:55.460 --> 00:51:57.980
which is that if you were
to assimilate them more,

00:51:57.980 --> 00:52:01.130
sort of push more of a
Swedish culture on them

00:52:01.130 --> 00:52:04.000
that would be against Swedish
nature in a bizarre way.

00:52:04.000 --> 00:52:05.750
Where America, we have a melting pot here

00:52:05.750 --> 00:52:07.710
so come here with all of your traditions

00:52:07.710 --> 00:52:10.880
and all of those things, but
mix into the fabric of America.

00:52:10.880 --> 00:52:14.970
Where Europe has more of a
ghettoization of culture.

00:52:14.970 --> 00:52:18.340
- This I think, the reason
America can do this better

00:52:18.340 --> 00:52:21.840
is because your country is
founded on the principle

00:52:21.840 --> 00:52:24.750
of individuality and individuals.

00:52:24.750 --> 00:52:29.260
Whereas Sweden is founded
on the idea of collectivism

00:52:29.260 --> 00:52:31.900
and that makes it really
hard to break the mold.

00:52:31.900 --> 00:52:35.090
Now I have a good friend,
he's doing a lotta work

00:52:35.090 --> 00:52:38.970
with newly arrived African boys

00:52:38.970 --> 00:52:41.420
and the top question,
this is Mustafa Panshiri,

00:52:41.420 --> 00:52:44.890
the question he's most
often asked by these guys

00:52:44.890 --> 00:52:47.237
is like, "How do I make Swedish friends?

00:52:47.237 --> 00:52:48.847
"I don't know, they never open up,

00:52:48.847 --> 00:52:50.470
"I'm never in touch with them."

00:52:50.470 --> 00:52:52.730
And at the same time, this is again,

00:52:52.730 --> 00:52:54.050
bringing tears to my eyes.

00:52:54.050 --> 00:52:55.120
They want to work.

00:52:55.120 --> 00:52:57.883
They want to break into becoming useful.

00:52:58.860 --> 00:53:00.257
At the same time Swedes
will be telling you,

00:53:00.257 --> 00:53:02.067
"Oh no, how you should behave?

00:53:02.067 --> 00:53:03.357
"No, I couldn't possibly tell you

00:53:03.357 --> 00:53:05.740
"just be yourself."
- Yeah, yes.

00:53:05.740 --> 00:53:07.490
- They give nothing away

00:53:07.490 --> 00:53:10.730
because they don't understand
being so collectivist.

00:53:10.730 --> 00:53:14.720
We have a very closed,
very complicated culture

00:53:14.720 --> 00:53:17.530
and if we want to invite
people into our culture

00:53:17.530 --> 00:53:21.347
we need to start, you know,
"Here we do it this way.

00:53:21.347 --> 00:53:26.347
"This is" you know, but that
is considered almost racist.

00:53:26.440 --> 00:53:29.417
Certainly socially
aggressive to tell people

00:53:29.417 --> 00:53:31.920
that, "Well this is how
we do things around here."

00:53:31.920 --> 00:53:35.020
- We take off our shoes before
we come into someone's home.

00:53:35.020 --> 00:53:36.780
That is quite unique.
- Yeah.

00:53:36.780 --> 00:53:38.670
- Yeah, it's us and the Japanese.

00:53:38.670 --> 00:53:39.710
Although we're more sloppy

00:53:39.710 --> 00:53:42.006
than the Japanese I think.
(Dave laughs)

00:53:42.006 --> 00:53:42.839
- And because this

00:53:42.839 --> 00:53:43.672
culture of--
- But there are all

00:53:43.672 --> 00:53:45.180
these unwritten rules,
of course there are.

00:53:45.180 --> 00:53:47.620
But for the longest
time Swedes denied that

00:53:47.620 --> 00:53:49.170
because it would be racist to admit

00:53:49.170 --> 00:53:51.100
we had our own culture.

00:53:51.100 --> 00:53:52.340
- Can you guys talk a little bit

00:53:52.340 --> 00:53:55.300
about how you differentiate from

00:53:55.300 --> 00:53:57.040
some of the other Nordic countries?

00:53:57.040 --> 00:53:59.720
Because as I said, we always
point to the Nordic countries

00:53:59.720 --> 00:54:02.400
but Sweden is the one
that we really focus on.

00:54:02.400 --> 00:54:03.890
But it sounds from what I can tell,

00:54:03.890 --> 00:54:06.310
and I did visit Denmark
and I visited Finland

00:54:06.310 --> 00:54:08.423
and a couple other places,

00:54:09.270 --> 00:54:11.000
Denmark doesn't seem to have the problems

00:54:11.000 --> 00:54:12.260
as much as you guys.

00:54:12.260 --> 00:54:16.080
- Well they did up until they
had those cartoonist scandals

00:54:16.080 --> 00:54:19.020
and then they sort of understood
what it was all about.

00:54:19.020 --> 00:54:21.290
If you can't criticize
Mohammed that's basically

00:54:21.290 --> 00:54:23.830
blasphemy laws and no modern Western state

00:54:23.830 --> 00:54:25.850
would stand for that.

00:54:25.850 --> 00:54:27.750
- I've had Flemming Rose
on who obviously you know

00:54:27.750 --> 00:54:30.660
is the publisher of the cartoons.

00:54:30.660 --> 00:54:32.800
And what an absolute brave person

00:54:32.800 --> 00:54:35.100
and someone who now has
to live unfortunately

00:54:35.100 --> 00:54:37.010
with a lifetime of security,

00:54:37.010 --> 00:54:40.130
who the idea that this
is a racist or a bigot

00:54:40.130 --> 00:54:42.680
is so patently absurd.
- Yes.

00:54:42.680 --> 00:54:45.490
- It was a Muslim author who was trying

00:54:45.490 --> 00:54:47.760
to find a cartoonist that
sparked the whole idea

00:54:47.760 --> 00:54:48.707
in the first place.
- Yeah, I know.

00:54:48.707 --> 00:54:51.110
- And he was trying to help, I mean it's--

00:54:51.110 --> 00:54:53.750
- But I also think culturally
over hundreds of years,

00:54:53.750 --> 00:54:56.040
Sweden and Denmark they've
fought for supremacy

00:54:56.040 --> 00:54:58.310
in Scandinavia and they sort of culturally

00:54:58.310 --> 00:55:01.120
define themselves in
opposition to each other.

00:55:01.120 --> 00:55:04.220
So Danes are more, they're
closer to the continent.

00:55:04.220 --> 00:55:06.050
They're more vivacious.

00:55:06.050 --> 00:55:07.830
They like to call a shovel a shovel,

00:55:07.830 --> 00:55:10.060
actually in Danish it's a spade a spade.

00:55:10.060 --> 00:55:11.993
But that would be wrong here I think.

00:55:14.005 --> 00:55:18.430
And Sweden is completely the
opposite, don't rock the boat.

00:55:18.430 --> 00:55:22.340
- Well if you look at this
from a historical perspective

00:55:22.340 --> 00:55:25.770
I think it's fair to say that Sweden

00:55:25.770 --> 00:55:30.120
was the Nordic super power in the 1600s.

00:55:30.120 --> 00:55:32.320
- Yes.
- We'd basically taken over

00:55:32.320 --> 00:55:33.900
the rest of the Scandinavian countries

00:55:33.900 --> 00:55:36.733
and then we kind of gradually
lost control of that.

00:55:37.720 --> 00:55:42.130
We gave Norway independence
and Denmark broke off.

00:55:42.130 --> 00:55:45.030
But the languages and the
culture is fairly similar.

00:55:45.030 --> 00:55:48.560
But Sweden's attitude has though remained

00:55:48.560 --> 00:55:52.620
as the stuck up big brother
that always knows best.

00:55:52.620 --> 00:55:54.810
I mean, we are a very arrogant culture

00:55:54.810 --> 00:55:55.990
if I can say so myself.

00:55:55.990 --> 00:55:59.330
I think it's pretty clear
that the Danes for instance,

00:55:59.330 --> 00:56:01.610
they think we're stuck up
and we're just plain wrong

00:56:01.610 --> 00:56:06.230
and now that we are, you know,
we've gone a bad way it's--

00:56:06.230 --> 00:56:08.250
- By now proven wrong.
- Right, right.

00:56:08.250 --> 00:56:10.530
- It is so embarrassing to admit it.

00:56:10.530 --> 00:56:12.327
So now it's like a situation where

00:56:12.327 --> 00:56:15.997
"No, I have to maintain
that I'm doing it this way

00:56:15.997 --> 00:56:17.587
"because it's too embarrassing to come out

00:56:17.587 --> 00:56:20.160
"to say, 'Okay, that was a
big mistake, I'm sorry.'"

00:56:20.160 --> 00:56:22.640
You know, the Danes are
putting up border controls

00:56:22.640 --> 00:56:24.229
against Sweden now because,
- Yeah, towards us.

00:56:24.229 --> 00:56:25.457
- "We don't want the problems you have

00:56:25.457 --> 00:56:28.590
"with bombs to be
exported into Copenhagen."

00:56:28.590 --> 00:56:31.100
- Right, but if you talk
about those problems

00:56:31.100 --> 00:56:33.030
- Exactly.
- Is there a lotta trouble?

00:56:33.030 --> 00:56:35.930
- No, the response when Denmark did that,

00:56:35.930 --> 00:56:37.840
the response from Swedish politicians

00:56:37.840 --> 00:56:40.537
was like, "Oh this is completely alarmist

00:56:40.537 --> 00:56:44.500
"but we welcome the Danes
to do what they please."

00:56:44.500 --> 00:56:46.380
So they were just saving face.

00:56:46.380 --> 00:56:49.140
- Yeah.
- But it's, I mean for Sweden

00:56:49.140 --> 00:56:53.710
which is one of the most
advanced IT service countries

00:56:53.710 --> 00:56:57.050
in the world, to have
to deal with the fact

00:56:57.050 --> 00:56:58.027
that people are saying, "We have to have

00:56:58.027 --> 00:56:59.797
"border (chuckles) controls
to you guys because there's

00:56:59.797 --> 00:57:02.800
"so much craziness
spilling into our country."

00:57:02.800 --> 00:57:05.080
- This analogy that you
mentioned of sort of

00:57:05.080 --> 00:57:06.820
a Hollywood facade on all this.

00:57:06.820 --> 00:57:08.590
As I said, it looks too
good on the outside,

00:57:08.590 --> 00:57:10.590
I really do think is part of the problem.

00:57:10.590 --> 00:57:12.500
It looks too good from the outside.

00:57:12.500 --> 00:57:15.050
Everyone looks too good
and everyone's clothes

00:57:15.050 --> 00:57:17.760
look too neat and new
and pressed and great

00:57:17.760 --> 00:57:19.670
and everyone looks sort of too healthy.

00:57:19.670 --> 00:57:20.503
And I guess that's not
(Henrik laughs)

00:57:20.503 --> 00:57:22.310
in every city, but it's
at least what's exported.

00:57:22.310 --> 00:57:25.830
- When we have a far
reaching eugenic programs

00:57:25.830 --> 00:57:27.210
that took care of that.
(Henrik chuckles)

00:57:27.210 --> 00:57:28.690
- That's probably a whole other show.

00:57:28.690 --> 00:57:30.620
- That's when you get guys like this.

00:57:30.620 --> 00:57:33.970
Look at the perfection.
(Dave laughs)

00:57:33.970 --> 00:57:35.690
- Is there anything else
that we didn't hit on

00:57:35.690 --> 00:57:39.863
sort of real meat of all of this?

00:57:39.863 --> 00:57:41.185
